  "plain": "This story is about a man named Donald Menzel and a set of papers known as the Majestic 12, or MJ12, documents. These papers are said to describe a top secret panel set up to study UFOs. An astronomer named Beatriz Villarroel, speaking with a podcast host, Jesse Michels, says that when you look into Menzel you suddenly find his name is famous because of these documents. She places this around the 1950s in the United States and does not say where she learned it. In a later episode, Michels tells it himself. He says Menzel was named in the MJ12 documents as a member of President Harry Truman's top secret UFO research panel, and he dates the panel to the late 1940s rather than the 1950s. Michels calls this something that adds to the mystery around Menzel. If it were true, it would mean a known public figure sat on a hidden government UFO panel."
